# J2: G1 at TP4 on all four cards, smoke and token agreement (run J2r first: it is the reference)
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the TP4 bring-up (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env, commit, and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig,
# a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# Duration (estimate, wall clock; the workflow's step limits in parentheses): reset 3-12 min; smoke: the first engine build compiles kernels and converts the 1x4 weight cache (20-50 min), then the API smoke 10-25 min, then agreement 5-10 min: about 60-110 min (step 210).
# The smoke's agreement test asks every prompt twice (with logprobs, sampled on the host; without, sampled on the device) and FAILS the step on an errored or incoherent answer, a device sampler that departs from the host's outside a bfloat16 near-tie, or a garbage perplexity. It cannot say the text is right: compare afterwards, on any machine: python3 scripts/ci/tp_agreement.py compare agreement-general-2link.json agreement-general-tp4.json (J2r's file first). TP4 sums in another order than TP2, so tokens are not bit-equal: the comparison judges the first place the two part (each side's token inside the other's top-5 and within half a nat), the perplexity ratio on both sides, and refuses (NOT_COMPARABLE) when the prompts differ. The profile runs the exact prefill conv beside the FIR audit for its first chunks (a mismatch stops the engine) and the fused prefill out-projection off (J2m runs it on).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-1
C2_PROFILE=general-tp4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,tool_call,stream_dropped,agreement
